# {{KIT_NAME}}

One sentence describing a requirement goes in; a working {{DS_NAME}} frontend comes out. That is the entire purpose.

## Before every UI task

Read the `{{DS_SLUG}}` skill. It describes the design system at a conceptual level—page anatomy,
layout, tokens, component selection—while the adjacent `craft.md` covers DS-independent craft
(states, motion, anti-patterns). Exact component APIs come from `design/components-meta.json` and
the source code under `src/components/`, never from memory.

There is deliberately only one skill. Missing knowledge belongs there, not in a second one.

## Structure

Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind, a single package, no workspace.

```
src/prototypes/<slug>/*.tsx    prototypes—create a file and its route exists (/p/<slug>)
src/prototypes/<slug>/_shared  shared shell/mock data for a prototype (not routed)
src/router.tsx                 automatic routing; do not modify
src/HomeView.tsx               automatic overview of all prototypes
src/components/                the {{DS_NAME}} components—use them, do not reinvent them
design/tokens.css              frozen tokens—never regenerate; edit only deliberately
design/components-meta.json    API source of truth: all components with props/variants
design/fixes.css               documented small corrections
.claude/skills/{{DS_SLUG}}/    the skill (+ craft.md)
```

## Commands

```bash
pnpm dev        # Port 5300
pnpm typecheck
pnpm export     # Static single-file export of all prototypes to export/index.html
```

If a development server for this kit is already running on the port, reuse it. Otherwise, start
your own and stop only your own process (by PID) when finished. Never terminate processes owned by
others, and never use `pkill` by name.

## Modes

- **proto** (default): build a specific idea as a clickable prototype. If the request
  describes a flow, build and link multiple screens.
- **ideate**: work divergently—create 3–5 deliberately distinct directions for a question as
  rough standalone screens under `src/prototypes/idea-<thema>-<variante>/` (keep the topic short and
  identical across all variants so the home page groups them). Use little detail and maximize the
  difference between approaches. State each direction's hypothesis in one sentence in the
  file-header comment. “Done means” applies in a reduced form: typecheck, console, and tokens still
  matter; complete states and flows only where they support the idea. The header/footer shell is
  optional; an unframed content screen is enough if the idea does not depend on its surroundings.
  The best direction is then developed into a complete prototype.

## Working approach

Do not ask what exactly the user means—build. Make assumptions visible in the prototype and
state them afterward instead of clarifying them first. The prototype is the question, not the answer.

Use realistic content: real domain terminology, plausible numbers, no Lorem Ipsum, and no
`Item 1/Item 2` lists. The prototype is judged by its content, not by its layout.

## Done means

1. `pnpm typecheck` passes.
2. Checked in a browser at a width of at least 1280px, with no console errors.
3. No hardcoded color or spacing value in the diff—everything comes from tokens.
4. Every flow has been clicked through once; empty, loading, and error states exist wherever they
   would exist in the real product.
